{title: Sing Hosanna}
{artist: David J. Ferguson}
{key: E}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: 98}

Verse 1
[E]Let not the wise man take pride in his knowing
[A]All the world’s wisdom won’t change where he’s going
[F#m]Rich men and strong men might boast of their kingdom
But [B]His praises matter, and we all must sing them, so
[E]Get yourself ready, stand up and proclaim Him
[A]Don’t be afraid to just speak out and name Him
[F#m]Go to your post and the task He will send you
[B]Don’t be afraid for the Lord will defend you

(Chorus x4 - harmonies build with each repeat)
[E]Ah-[D]ah, [A]sing hosanna to the [E]King
[E]Ah-[D]ah, [A]sing to our eternal [E]King

Verse 2
No [E]place at the banquet for stubborn self-righteous
In[A]vited instead, all the poor, lame and sightless
The [F#m]last will be first and the first will be last
And [B]one day we’ll find that when all else has passed
[E]Blessed are the meek, to a new home he sends them
[A]Blessed are the hurting, he comforts and mends them
[F#m]Trusting in Jesus, they’ve gained everything, so
They [B]shout out his praises, they dance and they sing to God

Chorus

(Break  x4 - building with each repeat)
[E]Sing hosanna, [D]sing hosanna,
[A]Sing hosanna to the [E]King

Chorus


